From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:11:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: verify Tristar fallback on IRQ storms

Keep the last verified limit if a storm-triggered fallback write or readback fails, and flag the discrepancy as unverified.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index 9e6381985..cfe8a36fb 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -1429,10 +1429,11 @@ static void tristar_source_event(struct tristar_charger *chg)
 		chg->storm_count = 0;
 	}
 	if (++chg->storm_count > TRISTAR_IRQ_STORM) {
-		dev_crit(chg->dev, "PMU source events storming; holding the fallback\n");
-		chg->chip->write_limit(chg, chg->chip->fallback_code);
-		WRITE_ONCE(chg->code, chg->chip->fallback_code);
 		WRITE_ONCE(chg->phase, TRISTAR_FAULT);
+		if (tristar_set_code(chg, chg->chip->fallback_code))
+			dev_crit(chg->dev, "PMU source events storming; input limit unverified\n");
+		else
+			dev_crit(chg->dev, "PMU source events storming; holding the fallback\n");
 		for (i = TRISTAR_IRQ_SOURCE; i < chg->nirqs; i++)
 			disable_irq_nosync(chg->irqs[i]);
 	}
